rule define_reach v1
description "A table over a define whose last row lies past what the define reaches: the check lets the row through, since E102 does not read the reach of a define, and a question over ranges of the inputs leaves it out"

enum band = small | big | huge

inputs
  amount : money[GBP]  range >=1GBP <=100GBP
  limit  : money[GBP]  range >=0GBP <=100GBP

outputs
  out : band

define excess : money[GBP] = amount - limit

table t
policy unique
| excess         | -> out : band |
| <=0GBP         | small         |
| >0GBP <=500GBP | big           |
| >500GBP        | huge          |

examples
| amount | limit  | -> out |
| 1GBP   | 100GBP | small  |
| 100GBP | 0GBP   | big    |
